  "definition": "Frequency of Monitoring for Regulated Inorganics",
  "effectiveDate": "2019-01-01",
  "historyNote": "#9700, eff 5-1-10; ss by #12668, eff 1-1-19",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Dw 711.04",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 711.04 Frequency of Monitoring for Regulated Inorganics",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 711.04 Frequency of Monitoring for Regulated Inorganics.\n\n(a) The O/O of a groundwater system shall collect one sample at each sample point during each 3-year compliance period.\n\n(b) The O/O of a surface water system, or combined surface/groundwater system, shall collect one sample at each sample point annually.\n\n(c) The frequency of monitoring for asbestos shall be as specified in Env-Dw 711.09 through Env-Dw 711.17.\n\n(d) The frequency of monitoring for nitrate and nitrite shall be as specified in Env-Dw 711.18 through Env-Dw 711.26.\n\n(e) The department shall waive the requirement for a community water system or non-transient, non-community water system to monitor for cyanide if the department determines that the PWS is not vulnerable to cyanide due to a lack of any industrial source(s) within the wellhead contributing area.\n\n(f) If the cyanide monitoring requirement is waived pursuant to (e), above, the O/O of each affected water system shall take not less than one sample every 9 years.\n\nSource. #9700, eff 5-1-10; ss by #12668, eff 1-1-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
}
